WEBVTT

00:05:58.482 --> 00:06:01.400
and then I directed it
for something like 21 years.

00:06:02.339 --> 00:06:05.029
If you were black
and African American and a dancer,

00:06:05.053 --> 00:06:07.379
any time between the '40s and the '70s,

00:06:07.403 --> 00:06:08.775
you had much to say,

00:06:08.799 --> 00:06:12.307
because your complete voice
was not being heard.

00:06:12.331 --> 00:06:15.783
And you were not being represented
as you truly were.

00:06:16.228 --> 00:06:18.593
Alvin Ailey had the courage,

00:06:18.617 --> 00:06:22.006
right in the middle
of the Civil Rights Movement,

00:06:22.030 --> 00:06:24.817
to present the truth about who we were --

00:06:24.841 --> 00:06:27.150
that our creativity, our beauty,

00:06:27.174 --> 00:06:29.325
our intelligence, our talents

00:06:29.349 --> 00:06:33.364
were an intrinsic part of the panoply
of American culture.